# GET /v1/models — GAISe-shaped model records.
#
# Works with the VS Code REST Client extension and the JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Start a server first, e.g.  HARRIER_MODELS=270m,0.6b target/release/harrier_api
#
# Each record: id, provider ("harrier"), display_name, status, capabilities, limits,
# plus an `embedding` profile (dimension_rule: fixed, task_control, resolved task_instructions)
# and `runtime` facts (architecture, source, device, dtype, load_seconds, default).

@host = http://localhost:3000

### All loaded models
# @name models
GET {{host}}/v1/models

### Filter by operation — `embeddings` (also `embedding`, `embed`) returns everything
GET {{host}}/v1/models?operation=embeddings

### Other GAISe operations are valid but this service offers none → empty list
GET {{host}}/v1/models?operation=instruct

### Filter by provider — `harrier` returns everything
GET {{host}}/v1/models?provider=harrier

### Any other provider → empty list
GET {{host}}/v1/models?provider=openai

### Both filters together, as a GAISe router would send them
GET {{host}}/v1/models?operation=embeddings&provider=harrier

### One model by GAISe-qualified id
# @name model
GET {{host}}/v1/models/harrier::harrier-oss-v1-0.6b

### One model by bare id
GET {{host}}/v1/models/harrier-oss-v1-270m

### One model by alias
GET {{host}}/v1/models/270m

###############################################################################
# Errors — plain-text bodies
###############################################################################

### 400 — unknown operation
GET {{host}}/v1/models?operation=bogus

### 404 — model that is not loaded
GET {{host}}/v1/models/harrier::harrier-oss-v1-27b
